AB  - The proceedings contain 29 papers. The special focus in this conference is on Business Process Modeling. The topics include: Multimodal Interpretable Feedback for Phlebotomy Training: A Conformance-Oriented Prototype with Time-Aligned Video and LLM-Based Reports; visualization Use in Process Mining Analysis; visually Retracing and Comparing Filter Steps in Exploratory Process Mining; Comparing the Comprehensibility of LLM-Generated and Human-Created Process Models: An Eye-Tracking Study; standing on the Shoulders of Giants: An Empirical Lens on Process Model Comprehensibility; the Cognitive Dimension of Exploratory Process Analysis: A Conceptual Vocabulary; causal Deviance Mining; on-the-Fly Event Disambiguation via Alignments; balanced Translucent Alignments; multitasking-Aware Estimation of Work-Item Duration via Proportional Overlapping-Time Redistribution; Functional Requirements for Wellbeing-Aware Resource Allocation in Industry 5.0 BPM Systems; From Agentic AI to Structured Workflows: Designing Process Architectures for AI-Augmented Administrative Decision Support; on the Alignment of Vibe Coding and Conceptual Models: An Exploratory Study with Base44; a Multi-dimensional Environment Metamodel for Model-Driven User Interface Development; modelDefenders: A Gamified Mutation Testing Tool for Model-Driven Engineering Education; an Ontology for Gender-Aware and Safe Business Process Management; separation of Concerns in Ontology-Driven Conceptual Modeling; an Assessment of Modelling Temporal Constraints in the e-Procurement Domain; Uncovering LLM’s Capabilities in Model-Based Question Answering for UML Class Diagrams; Evaluating LLM-Generated Finite State Machines: The Impact of Prompting Techniques on Structural and Semantic Accuracy; integrating Anticipation of Foreseeable Workarounds into Information System Engineering; modeling Culture’s Consequences - Enriching Enterprise Modeling with an Organizational (Sub-)Culture Perspective; operationalizing Futur