TI  - Leveraging Language Models for Automated Requirements to Design Transformation in MDA
AU  - Arystan, A.
T2  - Proceedings - 2026 18th International Conference on Electronics, Computer, and Computation, ICECCO 2026
AB  - Model-Driven Architecture (MDA) promises traceable development but still depends on manual translation of natural-language requirements into UML. The research describes an easy-to-use method which converts requirements into UML diagrams for the small multilingual Almaty pilot project. The system employs three main components which include a restricted intermediate JSON schema generated by a big language model (LLM) and PlantUML conversion through deterministic methods and XMI export for tool verification and basic rule-based comparison. The system evaluates structural extraction quality for vital UML elements by using precision/recall/F1 metrics which measure against a reference standard and assesses engineering value through XMI import success rates and human postediting time requirements. The following terms appear in this document: Model-Driven Architecture (MDA) and Requirements Engineering and Large Language Models (LLMs) and UML class diagrams and Model transformation and Accessibility. © 2026 IEEE.
