AB  - Alzheimer’s Disease (AD) diagnosis relies heavily on the identification and interpretation of various biomarkers. This research presents a novel framework for creating a comprehensive biomarker knowledge database for AD using Large Language Models. Our approach integrates advanced Natural Language Processing techniques with multiple state-of-the-art LLMs to extract, validate, and categorize biomarker information from clinical trials and medical literature. We demonstrate the effectiveness of our methodology through preliminary results in Named-Entity-Recognition. The pro-posed system aims to standardize biomarker terminology, establish relationship networks between biomarkers and clinical outcomes, and provide healthcare professionals with an accessible query-based interface to access AD biomarker research.
