AU  - M. I. A. Anshori
AU  - R. Yasirandi
AU  - I. M. Insan
T2  - 2025 IEEE 9th International Conference on Software Engineering & Computer Systems (ICSECS)
AB  - The digital transformation has heightened the demand for electronic signature systems. However, manual data entry during document upload remains error-prone and timeconsuming, hindering document management and verification. This study presents an enhancement to the Electronic Signature System at the Center of Excellence Technological Society (CAATIS) by integrating a Large Language Model (LLM) for automated document data extraction. Using the Llama 3.2 model deployed locally to ensure data privacy, the developed system automatically extracts key information such as titles, document reference numbers, descriptions, and names. Developed using the waterfall model, the solution demonstrated strong performance during testing, achieving F1-scores of 0.8974 for title extraction, 0.9688 for document reference number extraction, 0.8767 for document summarization, and a recall of 0.9112 for name extraction. Furthermore, the average document processing time was 5.15 seconds, satisfying all success metrics and quality requirements. These results meet the defined success criteria and demonstrate the potential of LLM integration to support more reliable electronic signature workflows. Furthermore, the developed document processing capabilities could be adapted and extended to other electronic signature systems.
