TI  - AssertSynth: LLM-Based Assertion Synthesis via Multimodal Specification Extraction
AU  - E. Tian
AU  - Y. Ci
AU  - Q. Yang
AU  - Y. Li
AU  - Z. Lyu
T2  - 2026 IEEE International Symposium on Circuits and Systems (ISCAS)
AB  - Assertion-Based Verification (ABV) is critical for ensuring functional correctness in modern hardware systems. However, manually writing high-quality SystemVerilog Assertions (SVAs) remains labor-intensive and error-prone. To bridge this gap, we propose AssertSynth, a novel unified framework that automatically synthesizes high-quality SVAs directly from multimodal hardware design specifications. AssertSynth employs a modality-aware preprocessing to parse heterogeneous specification formats (text, tables, diagrams, and formulas), followed by a set of dedicated semantic analyzers that extract structured representations aligned with signal-level semantics. These representations are utilized to drive assertion synthesis via multi-step chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting. The framework incorporates a mutation-based evaluation approach to assess assertion quality via model checking and further refine the synthesized assertions. Experimental evaluation across three real-world Register-Transfer Level (RTL) designs demonstrates AssertSynth’s superior performance, achieving an average increase of 8.4% in functional correctness and 5.8% in mutation detection compared to existing state-of-the-art approaches.
