AU  - B. Wang
AU  - X. Dong
AU  - Q. Song
AU  - H. Shi
T2  - 2025 6th International Conference on Artificial Intelligence and Computer Engineering (ICAICE)
AB  - This paper addresses the challenges of constructing a knowledge graph for civil aviation incidents, focusing on long entity lengths, the presence of hybrid and composite entities, and the similarities in form features of domain-specific entity names. We propose a method for building the civil aviation incident knowledge graph based on a multi-attribute attention alignment method using LLM twin networks. Structural similar entities from the civil aviation knowledge base are input into a "character embedding + fine-tuning layer" pre-trained language model (Embedding Pre-trained Language Models, EPLMs) for pre-training. By leveraging the characteristics of the twin network, a set of entities shares network weights during encoding, allowing the two sub-networks to acquire comprehensive semantic representations of entities and to determine the relative importance of each attribute.thereby improving the completeness of the civil aviation knowledge graph and enhancing the quality and standardization of the knowledge graph. Results from experiments show that the proposed model's F1 score is 96.72%. validating the model's effectiveness compared to other models.
