AB  - In the healthcare domain, the integration of medical data from diverse systems remains a persistent challenge due to the heterogeneity of standards and terminologies adopted by various institutions. This research proposes a semantic-based ontology mapping and merging approach exploring Large Language Models to enhance data interoperability across medical knowledge systems. The approach introduces context-enriched matching, which incorporates object and data property constraints to refine semantic correspondence. Through prompt engineering, LLMs are guided to evaluate logical and lexical similarity between medical entities. A case study involving laboratory record ontologies from two Saudi hospitals demonstrates the model's effectiveness in generating accurate semantic mappings, which can inform future ontology merging and enable more consistent querying and knowledge sharing. All related code, prompts, and mapping results are publicly available at: https://github.com/AyadSarah/One_EMR.
