AB  - Many students have several issues in pursuing their hobbies when they start careers after higher education. This paper presents a prototype design of mobile app that addresses this issue by assisting users in finding, learning, and maintaining their hobbies through relationships with friends and local communities. The app offers risk-aware advice and personalized recommendations for a variety of interests. It has capabilities for finding vendors and products, a conversational assistant driven by Large Language Model (LLM), and a mobile social environment. The app targets various kinds of users such as students, employees or businessmen. This research paper outlines HobbyHive's prototype design, implementation, and evaluation strategy, emphasizing how community design principles and Artificial Intelligence (AI) may boost hobby involvement while reducing risk through an awareness module. It also discusses implementation specifics, privacy and ethical issues, constraints, and potential future developments, such as sensor integration and Augmented Reality (AR) and Virtual Reality (VR) simulations for familiarizing users with high-risk hobbies.
