TI  - Knowledge Graph Augmented Retrieval Applications in Healthcare
AU  - C. A. Cogalan
AU  - A. Kumluca Topalli
T2  - 2025 Medical Technologies Congress (TIPTEKNO)
AB  - This paper reviews recent advances in knowledge graph–augmented retrieval for generation in healthcare. The focus is on how structured knowledge graphs can be integrated into retrieval pipelines to improve factual grounding, transparency, and clinical applicability. By linking clinical entities and relations to verifiable sources, knowledge graph–based retrieval reduces hallucinations, improves multi-hop reasoning, and enables auditability through explicit evidence paths and citations. Reported benefits include higher accuracy in laboratory test interpretation, more precise diagnostic reasoning, and improved personalization for under-represented patient groups. Several representative systems are compared to illustrate consistent design patterns, such as short graph paths and provenance tracking, which enhance stability and safety. The review highlights measurable improvements in accuracy, explainability, and equity across diverse clinical use cases. Overall, knowledge graph–guided retrieval augmented generation emerges as a promising approach for supporting decision-making, ensuring reliable evidence citation, and fostering safer adoption of generative AI in healthcare.
